// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/queen/replay/golden_chain_history.t27 -- the last 80 merged pull requests, landed by gc_land
; GENERATED from git and GitHub data. Do not edit by hand: regenerate it (below). The benchmark the
; actors rule asks for (see gHashTag/t27#7851) for queen/golden_chain.t27 (see #9027, #9029): the
; same 80 pull requests, merged into master from #8776 to #9082 (master a9ad52584016), once
; through gc_land and once as they really went on GitHub. This file holds gc_land's side as asserts.
; Window: master's last 80 first-parent commits, all pull request merges, in merge order. The pass's
; head is master before #8776, at #8775 (eb88ff84a0b2); it gets id 8775.
; One link per pull request, every stage golden (all of them merged):
; - id: the PR number. parent: the PR's merge-base with master (git merge-base <merge>^1 <PR head>),
;   mapped to the last window PR merged at or before it, else the head 8775.
; - edits (2012 rows over 1332 changed files): git diff -U3 --no-renames <merge-base> <PR head>.
;   A derived path is one GC_EDIT_DERIVED row (986 files): gen/ (policy/l2_generation.t27
;   is_gen), .trinity/seals/, docs/reports/t27b_expectations.json and bootstrap/stage0/FROZEN_HASH
;   (ci/derived_data.t27). An added, deleted, binary or wholly rewritten file is one EDIT_WHOLE row
;   (110 files). Every other hunk is EDIT_LINES over the base side, lo = old start,
;   hi = old start + old count (916 hunks in 236 files).
; - imports (134 rows): the `use` targets of the .t27 files each PR touched, read at its merge commit;
;   use a::b::c is specs/a/b/c.t27 when that file exists there, else specs/a/b.t27 (use_resolve.rs).
;   372 of 372 use lines resolved.
; - path ids: FNV-1a 64 of the UTF-8 path, low 52 bits (no collision among the window's paths).
; GCH_PARENT0 is the same window with each parent taken from the PR's first fork point instead,
; before any update merge or rebase: merge-base of <merge>^1 and the PR's first commit (the commit
; before the force push for #9055). It differs for 9 PRs.
; Regenerate: collect with git and gh only (gh api pulls/N, pulls/N/commits, issues/N/timeline;
; git fetch refs/pull/N/head; git merge-base, git diff, git show <merge>:<path>, git ls-tree <merge>),
; turn the diffs into rows on the lab, run `t27c gen-c specs/queen/golden_chain.t27` with a one-file C
; main that feeds these arrays to gc_land and prints out[] and the counts, and copy what it printed.
; The GitHub side of the same 80 PRs, measured from the API, the Actions runs and git, not asserted
; here (numbers on #7851 and #9027): 11 merges of master into a PR branch in 9 PRs and 2 force
; pushes (1 rebase, 1 amend); 5 of those merges conflicted (git merge-tree), 2 of them only in
; derived files; 4 extra full CI rounds on a PR that had already run CI. gc_land below: 0 REJUDGE,
; 0 CONFLICT. It reads each PR from its last merge-base, after GitHub's update merges, so the
; second test replays the first fork points.
; ASCII only (L3).
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

